globs: *.ds
alwaysApply: false
---

Destack is our custom high performance programming language.
It combines the performance of Rust with the ergonomics of Typescript.
It's inspired by Rust, Zig, Jai, GDScript, TypeScript, Swift.

We take from Rust a lot of the syntax, primitives and mechanisms.
We have modules with items, everything as an expression, traits, impls, structs.
Destack gets rid of all of Rust's borrow checking and macro system.
We have explicit enums, unions and tuples.

The macro system is lot closer to Zig comptime and Jai # but more refined. 
We don't have attributes like Rust but proper static functions, 
 which have the full power of regular functions.
Generally, you don't need to *define* your own macros, but you can use
 static features like #if, #for and such.

Type definition and inline function definitions should always be multiline. 

Unions (tagged sum types with `union`) in Destack are distinct from tag-only `enum`s.

References to Entities should usually happen through an EntityReference<...>.

Example program:
```
use destack::*;

/// Game state for the wordle game
enum WordleGameState {
	/// Game is ready to start
	Ready,
	/// Game is actively being played
	Playing,
	/// Game is paused
	Paused,
	/// Game over - player lost
	GameOver,
	/// Game won - word guessed correctly
	Victory
}

/// Letter state in a wordle guess
enum(string) WordleLetterState {
	/// Letter not yet guessed
	Empty = "Empty",
	/// Letter is in the word and in correct position
	Correct = "Correct",
	/// Letter is in the word but in wrong position
	Present = "Present",
	/// Letter is not in the word
	Absent = "Absent"
}

/// Error 
#error
union WordleError {
	OutOfLetters(u32),
	InvalidGuess({
		guess: String,
		reason: WordleLetterState,
		correct_word: String
	}),
	InvalidTargetWord(String, i32),
	InvalidGuessLength(u32),
	InvalidGuessFormat(String),
}

/// Base component for all wordle game objects
struct WordleComponent {
	is_active: bool = true,
}

/// A single letter cell in the wordle grid
struct WordleCell {
	/// The letter in this cell
	letter: Option<char> = None,
	state: WordleLetterState = WordleLetterState::Empty,
	isActive: bool = false,
}

/// A single guess row
struct WordleGuess<T: int> {
	/// The 5 letters in this guess
	cells: WordleCell[T],
	isSubmitted: bool = false,
	isCurrent: bool = false,
}

/// Keyboard key state tracking
struct WordleKeyState {
	/// The letter this key represents
	letter: char,
	/// State of this letter based on guesses
	state: WordleLetterState = WordleLetterState::Empty,
}

/// The main wordle game board
@entity(Entity) 
struct WordleBoard {
	use WordleComponent::*;
	
	guesses: WordleGuess[6],
	currentRow: u32 = 0,
	currentCol: u32 = 0,
	targetWord: String,
	isAcceptingInput: bool = true,
}

implement WordleBoard {
	function something(self) {
		// ...
	}
}

function somethingElse() {
	// ...
}

```